/*!
 * \page timertt_version timertt Version History
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_2_0 1.2.0
 *
 * \attention
 * Version 1.2.0 breaks compatibility with previous 1.0 and 1.1 versions.
 *
 * Some typedefs like timer_wheel_thread_t were removed (they were present
 * in v.1.1.* for compatibility with version 1.0).
 *
 * There is no more `timer_action` type. It is replaced by
 * `timertt::default_timer_action_type`.
 *
 * There is a possibility to specify a type of timer action as a template
 * parameter Timer_Action. By default the type of timer action is still
 * `std::function<void()>`.
 *
 * Scoped timer objects are introduced. These timer objects is not allocated
 * by timertt's timer_managers or timer_threads. A user creates them and
 * controlls their lifetimes. Something like:
 * \code
 * void f() {
 * 	timertt::default_timer_wheel_thread tt;
 * 	timertt::default_timer_wheel_thread::scoped_timer_object timer;
 * 	tt.start();
 * 	...
 * 	tt.activate(timer, std::chrono::milliseconds(250), []{...});
 * 	...
 * 	tt.shutdown_and_join();
 * }
 * \endcode
 *
 * New names: `timertt::default_timer_wheel_thread`,
 * `timertt::default_timer_heap_thread` and
 * `timertt::default_timer_list_thread` as an aliases for timer threads
 * with default template parameters.
 *
 * Some old compilers which has no decent support of C++11 can't compile
 * timertt now.
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_1_3 1.1.3
 *
 * Method empty() has been added to timer engines.
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_1_1 1.1.1
 *
 * New struct timertt::timer_quantities has been added.
 *
 * New methods get_timer_quantities() has been added to managers and
 * timer threads. Please note that get_timer_quantities() returns the count
 * of timers known to manager/thread. Some of that timers can be already
 * deactivated but not removed yet.
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_1_0 1.1.0
 *
 * A timer_managers have been introduced. They allow use timer inside just one
 * thread without necessity of creating additional working thread.
 *
 * For the most names in the library the naming convention have been changed:
 * suffix _t has been removed. Some names are kept intact for compatibility
 * with version 1.0 (for example: timertt::timer_t, timertt::timer_holder_t,
 * timertt::timer_wheel_thread_t,
 * timertt::timer_heap_thread_t,
 * timertt::timer_list_thread_t).
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_0_2 1.0.2
 *
 * Fix warning which is reported by some compiler at high warning level.
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_0_1 1.0.1
 *
 * Small code cleanup and improvement.
 *
 * \section timertt_version_1_0_0 1.0.0
 *
 * Initial release
 */

// vim:ft=cpp

